course: dictionary
lesson: 10295
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «A touchdown is worth six points, followed by a try for an extra point.» Points and try tell you this is a sport, so touchdown means a score.
explain: The same word can also describe something in the sky. When a plane or a Moon lander lands, that moment is called a touchdown. Ask yourself what is happening in the sentence: sport, flying or space?
explain: Clues can also come from where the word is used. In America and Canada, touchdown is the name for a football score. In rugby, the same kind of move is usually called a try.
fact: Touchdown is a noun, so you can have a touchdown or several touchdowns.
fact: In American and Canadian football, a touchdown is a score made by carrying or catching the ball over the other team's goal line.
fact: A touchdown in American football is worth 6 points.
fact: In rugby, putting the ball down over the line is also a touchdown, but it is usually called a try.
fact: When a plane or spacecraft lands on the ground, that moment is a touchdown.
exercise: «A touchdown is worth six points, followed by a try for an extra point.» What does touchdown mean here? | *A score in American football, worth 6 points | A plane landing on the runway | A ball thrown into the crowd | A gentle kick on the grass
exercise: «The spacecraft made a smooth touchdown on the Moon.» What does touchdown mean? | A loud noise high in space | *The moment a spacecraft lands on the ground | A try scored in rugby | A goal kicked in football
exercise: A boy in London says he loves football, and his friend in Chicago pictures helmets and touchdowns. Why did the friend get confused? | *Football means different games in different countries | Football means one game, the same everywhere | Helmets are only worn in rugby | Chicago has no football at all
test: In rugby, what is putting the ball down over the line usually called? | *A try | A goal | A field goal | A touchdown
test: «In American football a touchdown is 6; the kick after adds 1.» How many points is a touchdown worth? | 1 | 3 | *6 | 2
exam: Read this: «The plane made a smooth touchdown at dawn.» What does touchdown mean? | *The moment the plane landed on the ground | A ball put down over a rugby line | A kick over the bar | A score of 6 points in football
